Lolly patch 0006: Lolly's chrome over the editor.

Why: inside Lolly the editor wears Lolly's controls, built from the web
shell's own modules in Lolly's boot script (packages/rondo/editor/chrome.ts):
the audio transport, the visualiser switcher, the menus and context menus.
This hands that chrome what it drives (the editor, the audio session, the
library and the offline renders) through lolly.mountChrome, puts a gain
stage before the speakers so its volume and mute have something to turn,
tags each project row in the library with its id for the row's context
menu, gives the library the verbs of Lolly's Song menu (new, rename,
duplicate, start from an example), and leaves upstream's phone overflow menu
unmounted (Lolly's menus
carry those controls). The WebGPU shader visuals (src/shaderviz/) are not
mounted: Lolly's MilkDrop visualiser takes their place (decision D4 of plan
301). Upstream's header stays in the page, unseen, so its panels and
popovers still open from Lolly's menus. With no host the app is unchanged.

Applied by scripts/vendor-rondocode.ts with git apply --directory=packages/rondo/upstream.

